      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Amino pyridine-based rhodamine conjugate (APR) has been developed as a first chemosensor for selective detection and quantification of L-4-Hydroxyproline (Hyp). The \"turn-on\" fluorescence property of the chemosensor makes it unique for easy estimation of Hyp in collagen and biological samples."},
